# Client deliverables

Files under `docs/deliverables/` and `docs/draft/` are presentation material that **leaves the repo for the client**. The client does not know this internal repository or its folder layout.

Full context: `docs/deliverables/README.md` (promoted deliverables) and `docs/draft/README.md` (drafts in progress).

> **Sibling rule**: `.cursor/rules/deliverable-draft-workflow.mdc`
> (how to compose and regenerate the Pandoc `.docx` draft under `docs/draft/`).
> This rule covers **what must not appear** in client-facing content; the other covers **composition process**. Keep them aligned if you change either.

## Principle

These folders are **not canonical.** Any new or confirmed information here must be **ported first** to the appropriate canonical file
(Archi model, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/architecture-gaps-and-questions.md`, etc.).
The deliverable reflects what is already backed up, not the other way around.

## Canonical sources by information type

| Information | Canonical file |
|-------------|------------------|
| AS-IS model (actors, apps, APIs, nodes, relations) | Archi + `docs/diagrams/{{ARCHIMATE_EXPORT_FILENAME}}` |
| Narrative architecture | `ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Technical C4 diagrams | `docs/diagrams/drawio/*.drawio`, `docs/diagrams/puml/*.puml` (derived from Archi or `ARCHITECTURE.md`) |
| Implementation / publication flows | `docs/diagrams/puml/flow-*.puml` (+ Draw.io under `drawio/` when present) |
| Gaps, open questions, meeting confirmations | `docs/architecture-gaps-and-questions.md` |
| Scope and objectives ({{INITIATIVE_ID}}) | `SPEC.md` |
| Operational backlog | `backlog.md` + `backlog/tasks/` |
| Minutes and action items | `backlog/meetings/AAAA-MM-DD-*.md` |
| Raw immutable transcripts | `transcripts/` (see `transcripts-immutable.mdc`) |
| Client-provided documentation | `docs/client-documentation/` |

## Critical rule · No internal project references

When editing anything under `docs/deliverables/` or `docs/draft/` (diagrams,
`.md` annexes, PPTs, PDFs, future docs):

**Forbidden:**
- Internal repo paths: `docs/…`, `docs/client-documentation/…`,
  `.cursor/…`, `docs/diagrams/…`, `backlog/…`, `transcripts/…`,
  or any path that exposes this repository layout.
- Internal working filenames: `architecture-gaps-and-questions.md`,
  `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `SPEC.md`, `backlog.md`, `{{ARCHIMATE_EXPORT_FILENAME}}`,
  `archi-server MCP`, etc.
- Mentions of this internal repository by vendor or tool name, rules (`.cursor/rules/…`), internal-only meetings,
  internal methodology decisions.

**Allowed when citing client material:**
- The **relative path inside documentation the client gave you**,
  starting from the folder/space name **as the client uses it**.
- The **file or image name alone**, when enough.
- The **Confluence space or logical folder name** as the client knows it.

**Never prefix with** `docs/client-documentation/…` **or any internal repo path.**

## How to proceed

1. Before changing a file in `docs/deliverables/` or `docs/draft/`, confirm the information already exists in a canonical file. If not, port it there first.
2. When citing client material, use the path **as the client names it** (never our internal repo path).
3. When citing internal consulting-only material: do not cite it. Use neutral wording backed by the client or a placeholder like "⚠ Revisar este punto".
4. If unsure whether a reference is internal-only, ask the user before writing.

